      D2. Verdict child shape (pin)
      ════════════════════════════════════
      On an applied archived
      bundle, the Verdict this
      write appends has one child
      per complete CloseEvidence
      AC-*. The child tag is that
      AC-* id. Its children are
      Exit (decimal exit-code text)
      and Result (pass or fail).
      No attributes on the AC-*
      child (anchors stay
      attribute-free). Example
      shape, names binding:

        Verdict outcome=pass
          AC-EXAMPLE
            Exit 0
            Result pass

      Existing Verdicts with no
      children stay valid. This
      bundle does not add a
      forbid-unknown-Verdict-child
      validator (that would be a
      fourth T-001 red or a sixth
      task). A later validator that
      rejects unknown Verdict
      children must keep this
      shape legal. T-001 may
      export a reader for this
      shape; T-003 writes it;
      T-004 reads it.

